rk` returned equal output for empty, partial and extra-space mark dictionaries. Hash/byte comparisons confirmed the text-copy and budget facts above.\n\nCoverage against Done-when, in specification order:\n\n| Item | Independently observed coverage or remaining obligation |\n|---|---|\n| Spine meaning and IF-101 | SR-174 retains its original three acceptance clauses and adds reservation behavior; LLR-362/363 and TC-401/402 express the intended split. Interface and code bindings need findings below. |\n| One checkpoint and applicable acts | UNCOVERED at this tip: four new rows remain Drafted and this diff contains no corresponding approval acts. Changed SR-174/TC-158 still owe scoped re-attestation; this review does not perform it. |\n| Reserve argument table, no writes on refusal | `test_each_reserve_refusal_writes_nothing` and usage-error test drive the CLI and compare both durable states. |\n| First carrier commit, CAS and lost race | First-reservation and lost-race repository tests; additional simultaneous-process probe confirmed actual ref-lock behavior. |\n| Sequential/stale-base ranges and correction floor | Three named repository tests; sequential case fails on the pre-lane implementation. |\n| Clean/conflicted fold | Pure maximum/record-union cases and `test_fold_ids_on_a_conflicted_watermark`. |\n| Hand raise, all-parent append-only records, writers, correction grammar | Added `test_id_watermark.py` cases drive the integrity CLI and both writers; old regression assertions remain. |\n| Landing table on both callers | Parameterized slot/squash cases, unreadable claims, retired-in-own-range and code-only controls. UNCOVERED dispatcher-before-refresh collision case, reproduced in finding 1. |\n| Landing fold and watermark-only refresh conflict | Actual slot, squash and refresh tests, including a moved carrier and refusal/rollback with another conflict. |\n| Act ledger, numbering and latch unchanged | No implementation delta to those mechanisms; selected rejudge/adjudication tests ran. This is not a claim to have run the unrequested act-suite modules. |\n| Keep-or-mint and byte restamp | PROCESS paragraph, measured +457 bytes and correct matching stamps. |\n| Spine-questions citation | Changed §0 citation inspected; one rule home retained. |\n| Spine-author reserved ranges / shortage behavior | Actual prompt text inspected and new prompt test passed; no watermark-counting or bump instruction remains. |\n| Coordinator reserve/rebase/latch text and copies | Recipes and skill inspected; byte-identical shipped/agents/claude copies and passing prompt pins. |\n| RESYNC entry and upgrade route | One entry covers new module, scripts/hook, open-lane renumbering, record preservation and squash behavior, including the unclaimed feature-branch restriction. |\n| Own IDs reserved; other open lanes named at landing | UNCOVERED at this tip: `git show refs/heads/id-carrier:docs/id-watermark` reports no such ref; the committed watermark has no reservation records. Landing-time reservation/renumbering and other-lane census remain required. |\n| Generated pages | Prompt catalog updated. Other named pages are landing-time generation obligations, not evidenced as regenerated by this diff. |\n| Commit bar and both strict lints | Prescribed replacement suite and strict trajectory/integrity results quoted above. No full/smoke suite or separate `trace.py --strict` was run; an unconditional green-bar claim is unsupported here. |\n| OI-116 | Spec records the spine-only owner answer; code retains trunk-only WI/OI/DP writers. |\n\nSemantic relationship decisions: retain unchanged SN-025/SN-027 acceptance and approval. Keep SR-174's identity: its original work-item allocation/reuse obligations survive the widening. Retain LLR-153 and its TC-147 because they independently verify the trunk WI mint, including replay/deleted-identity behavior; retain LLR-154 and TC-148 because they independently verify the serialized post-merge intake invocation. Further splitting either would repeat its single ownership/invocation decision, rather than introduce an independent obligation. Retain SR-170/SR-173's references: exclusive writing and transactional regeneration still differ from allocation. Carry the reservation extension into TC-158 and IF-101, whose tests/callers now consume it; repair IF-101's inaccurate surface, rather than treating reference existence as semantic agreement. IF-173's changed readiness name matches dispatch's caller; its compact registry description still identifies the same library surface. IF-257's retirement-file schema remains unchanged by the additional tree reader, so retain that counterpart.\n\nFor the new decomposition, retain LLR-362 as the durable allocation-record lifecycle: allocation, monotonic reservation authority and preservation are the producer/storage sides of that same record. TC-401 verifies allocation/concurrency/fold behavior; TC-158 independently verifies commit-integrity and writer preservation. Retain LLR-363 as the admission decision shared by both landing routes, with TC-402 verifying actual acceptance/refusal and fold integration. These separate allocation from use: either can fail while the other succeeds. Splitting individual argument cases, git plumbing calls, or route adapters would add no independent decision. The admission failure contradicts sound SR-174 acceptance; PROCESS §5 calls for correcting the owning admission design, including an LLR-363 amendment if needed, while preserving parent acceptance/approval and enduring behavioral tests. It does not justify weakening the promised reservation rule. Any changed child text still requires its applicable independent act.\n\nFindings:\n\n- [MAJOR] project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py:3359 -> [K1, B1; SR-174/LLR-363] The lane's moving merge base erases an unreserved addition before the dispatcher judges it: after the legitimate owner lands SR-006, `_drain` speculatively refreshes the other lane that also drafted SR-006; `_reserved_id_refusal` then sees SR-006 in both tip and base and admits it. The real claims/reserve/land/drain reproduction initially refuses WI-401 and subsequently merges it with drain exit 0, despite its sole reservation being SR-007 -> Make reservation admission own the lane's introduced-ID attribution before refresh can absorb trunk content, and preserve that attribution through landing; add a dispatcher-level regression with two real reservations and the first owner's successful landing, preserving refusal of the second author's collision. This moves validation to the single owning admission boundary rather than adding a compensating post-refresh guard (antidote, .agents/skills/antidote/SKILL.md) -> @implementer convergence-class: yes\n- [MINOR] docs/requirements/interfaces.toml:1388 -> [K1, B1; PROCESS §8] IF-101 advertises `fold_ids`, which has no definition; the implemented and documented call is `fold_watermark`. Its Data cell also grew to 405 characters against the declared 160-character surface limit and repeats behavioral contract prose -> Replace Data with a compact, accurate surface/schema pointer naming the actual exported calls, retaining the detailed guarantees in the owner's IF-101 contract -> @implementer\n- [MINOR] docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml:3749 -> [K3] The new LLR bindings do not match the built code: LLR-362 omits tagged functions including `reserve`, `carried` and `record_history_findings`; `id_carrier.landing_refusal` and its landing helpers are tagged LLR-362, while the landing obligation is LLR-363 and that row omits id_carrier.py from its modules -> Reconcile the two new rows' Module/Code-Symbol fields and function Implements tags against the final allocation/admission ownership, so the landing code traces to its actual obligation; reconcile the Drafted rows before their independent approval -> @implementer\n- [MINOR] project-trajectory/scripts/trace.py:1687 -> [B1; PROCESS §3, Consolidate, don't duplicate] `_render_full` rebuilds every space with a zero default and delegates to `render_watermark`, whose body already iterates exactly WATERMARK_SPACES with the same zero default; the wrapper adds no behavior and repeats the renderer's responsibility -> Delete `_render_full` and call the existing renderer directly at its two callers, preserving the established argument order -> @implementer\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=4\n36:- Landing folds the carrier, and a refresh conflict is resolved by the fold: test_the_slot_folds_a_carrier_moved_after_the_lanes_refresh, test_a_hand_squash_folds_a_carrier_moved_after_the_lanes_fold, test_a_refresh_conflicting_only_on_the_watermark_is_resolved_by_the_fold and test_the_dispatchers_drain_refreshes_a_lane_whose_watermark_lags_the_carrier.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f031c6a5-ecf0-490f-9890-c7a8a87f92fc","uuid":"37eab024-7543-410e-a8b3-82f95013bb02","timestamp":"2026-11-02T17:12:05.944Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Reviewed: 82e4ca1a73bc48382f04522c3f71a3ac811048ad\n\nVerified: The checkout matched the reviewed commit. Reviewed the scoped three-dot diff, WI-978 and its item-16 specification, PROCESS §§3–6/8, the kit-change rubric, and the affected registry rows and historical counterparts. Hunted reservation-admission fail-open first, then watermark loss/reuse and incorrect folds. Real concurrent reserve processes in two worktrees produced one successful allocation and one lost-CAS refusal, with only the winner recorded. Sequential/stale-base allocation, correction floors, record preservation and both landing routes have substantive executable coverage. Coordinator copies match, PROCESS grew by the declared 457 bytes, and the byte-budget skill copies are each 4,527 bytes. The dispatcher nevertheless admits a collision after refresh, reproduced through actual claims, reservations and landings below. No reviewed source was edited; no repository commit was made.\n\nCommands:\n\n- `git rev-parse HEAD`; `git 